@startuml
' One pipeline run + the human write path, as swimlanes.
' GitHub does not render PlantUML inline — open this file in PlantUML/Kroki.

title Pipeline run: new Immich photo -> proposals -> confirmed write

|Immich|
|reid-trigger / reid-ui|
|reid-core (job manager)|
|reid-batch subprocess|
|local store|
|operator (review UI)|

|reid-trigger / reid-ui|
:nightly systemd timer\nor "Run now" in the UI;
|reid-core (job manager)|
:POST /api/jobs;
:start run (run_status = running,\nREID_RUN_ID set, one run at a time);
:spawn "python -m reid.cli --config reid.toml";
|reid-batch subprocess|
:read checkpoint;
|local store|
|reid-batch subprocess|
:fetch the new-asset feed;
|Immich|
:POST /api/search/metadata\n(createdAfter = checkpoint, type = IMAGE);
|reid-batch subprocess|
:for each new asset;
|Immich|
:GET /api/assets/{id}/thumbnail?size=preview\n(or /original when pixel_source = original);
|reid-batch subprocess|
:YOLO11n person detection;
:quality gates, in order —\nconfidence floor, then min box height\n(edge-clipped boxes are kept);
:OSNet-AIN x1.0 embed of the full-person crop\n(512-dim, L2-normalized float32);
|local store|
:replace appearances per asset;
|reid-batch subprocess|
:cluster + anchor over ALL stored appearances;
:exclude operator-ignored appearances\nand appearances with no usable capture time;
:tombstone detection — ledger pairs no longer\nlabeled in Immich become tombstones;
|Immich|
:GET /api/faces?id=... for each appearance-bearing asset;
|reid-batch subprocess|
:partition capture days (EXIF, local tz,\nfallback upload time) into timespan windows;
:per window — cosine distance matrix,\naverage-linkage clustering cut at distance_threshold;
:anchor each cluster — a face claims an appearance at\nface_overlap containment (best match wins),\nunanimous name = proposed, 2+ names = conflicted,\nnone + size >= min_cluster_size = ask_for_name,\npins override, operator rejections drop proposals;
|local store|
:replace proposals wholesale,\nupdate run_status.windows_done per window;
:advance checkpoint to newest createdAt\n(only after the whole run succeeds);
|reid-core (job manager)|
:run_status = done / failed / cancelled\n(confirmations and writes refused while running);
|operator (review UI)|
:review queue — Proposals and Final check tabs;
:confirm / dismiss cluster, reject appearance-name pair,\npin appearance, ignore detection\n(persist as review decisions — no Immich writes here);
|reid-core (job manager)|
:POST /api/write-faces\n(needs idle core + write-scoped API key);
:per item — skip if ignored or rejected,\nresolve person by name (find or create),\nresolve head box (Immich unassigned face contained\nin the person box, else SCRFD-500M fallback on the crop),\nchecks in order — write ledger, tombstone,\nconflict / already labeled, no head found;
|Immich|
:POST /api/faces (assetId, personId, head box);
|local store|
:journal write_ledger entry -> "written";
|reid-batch subprocess|
:next run — labels the user removed in Immich\nbecome tombstones and are never re-proposed;
@enduml
